  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nLyon County, Iowa - County Government\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSkip to content\n\n\n\n \n \n\n \n \n \nLyonCounty · Iowa\n \n \n\n Bid Notices\n Calendar\n\n Courts\n\n Employment\n FAQ\n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n About \n \n\n Communities\n Elected Officials\n School Districts\n Township Information\n \n \n \n\n Departments \n \n\n Assessor\n Attorney\n Auditor & Elections\n Community Services\n Conservation\n Economic Development\n Emergency Management\n Engineering & Secondary Roads\n Public Health\n Recorder\n Sheriff\n Treasurer\n Veterans Service Office\n Zoning\n \n \n Supervisors\n Contact\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n Clear · 50°\n \n \n\n \n Find departments, services, staff, and more\n \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n Photo Credit: Jeremy Stiltz\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n General Election \n \n \n\n \n \n Economic Development \n \n \n\n \n \n Lake Pahoja \n \n \n\n \n \n Meetings & Agendas \n \n \n\n \n \n Beacon/Real Estate \n \n \n\n \n \n Renew Vehicle Tags \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \nWelcome to Lyon County, Iowa \n \n\nLyon County was formed in 1872 from sections of Woodbury County. It's home to eight communities, four school districts, and 11,934 residents. The County is administered by a five-member Board of Supervisors who are elected for four-year terms. Other elected officials include the Attorney, Auditor, Recorder, Sheriff, and Treasurer. \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \nWhat's Happening\n \n\n \n\n \n\n Oct \n \n\n 20 \n \n \n\n Coffee with Conservation - Bites, Brews & Living Fossils!\n 11:30am\n Lyon County Nature Center · 1651 180th Street · Inwood, IA \n \n\n \nCoffee with Conservation - Bites, Brews & Living Fossils!\n Lyon County Nature Center\n 1651 180th Street\n Inwood, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n October 20, 2026 to January 1, 3000 \n 11:30am · 12:30pm \n\nBites, Brews & Living Fossils! \n \n\nDid you know prehistoric river giants are swimming right here in our backyard? Join us for Lunch & Living Fossils—a special edition of Coffee With Conservation featuring guest speakers from the Iowa DNR Fisheries team! \n \n\nSwap your desk lunch for an incredible story of local conservation. We’re providing free sandwiches, coffee, and cold drinks while learning all about the historic reintroduction of paddlefish to the Iowa Great Lakes! \n \n\nGrab a lunch plate and discover: \n \n \n \nHow paddlefish survived over 100 million years of history \n \nThe exciting work Iowa DNR is doing to restore paddlefish to West Okoboji & local waters \n \nThe secret \"electric paddle\" snout they use to hunt underwater \n \nWhat it takes to protect these massive native filter-feeders \n \n \n\nWhere: Lyon County Nature Center    1651 180th St.  Inwood, IA 51240 \n \n\nWhen: October 20th at 11:30 AM    \n \n\nCost: Free! (Sandwiches, coffee, and drinks provided) \n \n\nBring a friend, grab a sandwich, and meet the DNR experts bringing these ancient giants back to our lakes! \n \n\n  \n \n\nFree, but please register by calling (712) 752-2033 or calling or texting 712-470-9693 to ensure we have enough goodies for everyone!! \n \n\nRegister at https://lyoncounty.iowa.gov/conservation/events/  \n \n\n  \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n Nov \n \n\n 3 \n \n \n\n Nature Tales - Rock Rapids Public Library, November 3rd, 2026\n 4:30pm\n Rock Rapids Public Library · 102 S Greene St. · Rock Rapids, IA \n \n\n \nNature Tales - Rock Rapids Public Library, November 3rd, 2026\n Rock Rapids Public Library \n 102 S Greene St.\n Rock Rapids, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n November 3, 2026 to January 1, 3000 \n 4:30pm · 12:00am \n\nStep into the quiet, winter woods and discover a hidden universe thriving right beneath our feet! Inspired by Kate Messner’s acclaimed book Over and Under the Snow, this hands-on STEM program takes young explorers deep into the subnivean zone—the cozy, secret world where mice tunnel, bullfrogs sleep, and wildlife survives the freeze. \n \n\nWhat You'll Experience: \n \n \n \nExplore the Hidden Layers: Uncover how snow acts like a giant blanket to keep animals warm all winter long. \n \nTrack the Predators: Compare the hunters above the snow—like foxes and snowy owls—with the secret survivors underneath. \n \n \n\nGrab your field journal, put on your scientist hat, and discover what's really happening under the winter frost! Perfect for curious minds, families, and homeschool groups ages 5 and up. \n \n\nWhere: Rock Rapids Public Library \n \n\nWhen: November 3rd at 4:30 PM \n \n\nAdmission: FREE! No registration required. \n \n\nThe forest is full of secrets—come see what’s living under the snow! \n \n\n  \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n Nov \n \n\n 4 \n \n \n\n Nature Tales - George Public Library, November 4th, 2026\n 3:00pm\n George Public Library · 119 S. Main Street · George, IA \n \n\n \nNature Tales - George Public Library, November 4th, 2026\n George Public Library \n 119 S. Main Street\n George, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n November 4, 2026 to January 1, 3000 \n 3:00pm · 12:00am \n\nStep into the quiet, winter woods and discover a hidden universe thriving right beneath our feet! Inspired by Kate Messner’s acclaimed book Over and Under the Snow, this hands-on STEM program takes young explorers deep into the subnivean zone—the cozy, secret world where mice tunnel, bullfrogs sleep, and wildlife survives the freeze. \n \n\nWhat You'll Experience: \n \n \n \nExplore the Hidden Layers: Uncover how snow acts like a giant blanket to keep animals warm all winter long. \n \nTrack the Predators: Compare the hunters above the snow—like foxes and snowy owls—with the secret survivors underneath. \n \n \n\nGrab your field journal, put on your scientist hat, and discover what's really happening under the winter frost! Perfect for curious minds, families, and homeschool groups ages 5 and up. \n \n\nWhere: George Public Library \n \n\nWhen: November 4th at 3:00 PM \n \n\nAdmission: FREE! No registration required. \n \n\nThe forest is full of secrets—come see what’s living under the snow! \n \n\n  \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n Nov \n \n\n 12 \n \n \n\n Nature Tales - Larchwood Public Library, November 12th, 2026\n 4:00pm\n Larchwood Public Library · 1020 Broadway Street · Larchwood, IA \n \n\n \nNature Tales - Larchwood Public Library, November 12th, 2026\n Larchwood Public Library \n 1020 Broadway Street\n Larchwood, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n November 12, 2026 to January 1, 3000 \n 4:00pm · 12:00am \n\nStep into the quiet, winter woods and discover a hidden universe thriving right beneath our feet! Inspired by Kate Messner’s acclaimed book Over and Under the Snow, this hands-on STEM program takes young explorers deep into the subnivean zone—the cozy, secret world where mice tunnel, bullfrogs sleep, and wildlife survives the freeze. \n \n\nWhat You'll Experience: \n \n \n \nExplore the Hidden Layers: Uncover how snow acts like a giant blanket to keep animals warm all winter long. \n \nTrack the Predators: Compare the hunters above the snow—like foxes and snowy owls—with the secret survivors underneath. \n \n \n\nGrab your field journal, put on your scientist hat, and discover what's really happening under the winter frost! Perfect for curious minds, families, and homeschool groups ages 5 and up. \n \n\nWhere: Larchwood Public Library \n \n\nWhen: November 12th at 4:00 PM \n \n\nAdmission: FREE! No registration required. \n \n\nThe forest is full of secrets—come see what’s living under the snow! \n \n\n  \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n Nov \n \n\n 17 \n \n \n\n Coffee with Conservation - Binoculars, Brews & Bites! \n 11:30am\n Lyon County Nature Center · 1651 180th Street · Inwood, IA \n \n\n \nCoffee with Conservation - Binoculars, Brews & Bites! \n Lyon County Nature Center\n 1651 180th Street\n Inwood, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n November 17, 2026 to January 1, 3000 \n 11:30am · 12:30pm \n\nBinoculars, Brews & Bites!  \n \n\nLooking for the ultimate mid-day break? Join us for Brews & Binoculars—now served with lunch! Swap your lunch desk for the outdoors and learn the basics of local birdwatching over fresh sandwiches and cool drinks. \n \n\nGrab a lunch plate and come learn:  Quick tricks to dial in binoculars fast.  How to identify birds by shape, size, and markings. Simple tips for birding by ear.  How to use cool apps like Merlin Bird ID to track what you see \n \n\nWhere: Lyon County Nature Center    1651 180th St.  Inwood, IA 51240 \n \n\nWhen: November 17th at 11:30 AM    \n \n\nCost: Free! (Sandwiches, coffee, and drinks provided + loaner binoculars available) \n \n\nBring a friend, grab a sandwich, and let’s spot some feathered friends! \n \n\n  \n \n\nFree, but please register by calling (712) 752-2033 or calling or texting 712-470-9693 to ensure we have enough goodies for everyone!! \n \n\nRegister at https://lyoncounty.iowa.gov/conservation/events/  \n \n\n  \n \n\n \n \n \n\n View the Full Calendar\n \n \n\n \nTrending\n \n\n \n1\n \nReal Estate Search\n \n \n\n \n2\n \nEmployment\n \n \n\n \n3\n \nDepartments and Officials\n \n \n\n \n4\n \nElections and Voting\n \n \n\n \n5\n \nCourts\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n Stay connected with Lyon County\n \nThings to Know\n \n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n\n \nSeptember 25\n \n \n\n Employment\n \n4 Job Openings\n \n \n \n \n\n \nDecember 2\n \n \n\n Engineering & Secondary Roads\n \nSnow Ordanance\n \n \n \n \n\n \nNovember 3\n \n \n\n Engineering & Secondary Roads\n \nPUBLIC NOTICE\n \n \n \n\n\n\n News Employment Bid Notices Notifications\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n Lyon County Recreation\n \nLake Pahoja\n Learn More\n \n \n\n \nLake Pahoja Recreation Area is a 300 acre highly developed multi-use recreation area. It offers a wide variety of activities for all seasons. \n \n\nA few of the features at Lake Pahoja include 6 open picnic shelters with modern restroom facilities and drinking water available, three playgrounds, two volleyball courts, a basketball court, and horseshoe pits. Two enclosed lodges are also available - each containing four to six picnic tables, a fireplace, and outdoor pedestal grills. \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nLyon County Courthouse\n\n 206 S. 2nd Ave.\n\n Rock Rapids, IA 51246\n\n Contact Us\n \n\n Lyon\n County • Iowa\n \n \nCourthouse Hours\n\n M - F 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.\n Closed Holidays\n\n Department Hours May Vary\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n©2026 Lyon County, Iowa · Title VI Nondiscrimination Policy\n \npowered by \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nUpcoming Holiday Closure Schedule\n \n \nChristmas Eve-Office's Close at 12:00 PM (December 24, 2026)\n \nChristmas Day (December 25, 2026)\n \n\n\n\n"
}
